<title>UK: UK budget increases 1997 BSE elimination fund.</title>
<headline>UK budget increases 1997 BSE elimination fund.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>An additional 736 million stg in funding in 1997 to eliminate Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE) from UK cattle herds was was announced by UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke in his November budget speech on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The budget also gave support of 60 million stg for the UK's 60,000 upland farmers through increased the Hill Livestock Compensation Allowance (HLCA) payments, according to a Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Food announcement.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8058</p>
</text>
